# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored except this file.
#
# Every assignment below is commented out deliberately. An environment variable
# that exists but is *empty* is not the same as an unset one, and a blank value
# has broken this build before — so uncomment a line only when you have a real
# value for it.

# Canonical origin used by metadata, robots.txt and sitemap.xml.
# Without it the site advertises http://localhost:3000 in every canonical URL,
# OpenGraph tag and sitemap entry.
# A bare domain is accepted — `your-domain.com` is read as `https://your-domain.com`.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# --- Contact form -----------------------------------------------------------
# Leave RESEND_API_KEY unset and the form needs no account at all: it hands the
# visitor a prefilled `mailto:` link instead of sending. Set it to deliver
# messages by email — see "Contact form" in README.md.
# Create a key at https://resend.com/api-keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx

# Where contact messages are delivered. Defaults to the address in
# src/data/site.ts, so it is normally fine to leave unset.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# The sender. Resend only accepts a `from` address on a verified domain.
# `onboarding@resend.dev` is Resend's shared test sender: it works immediately
# but only delivers to the address that owns the Resend account. Replace it with
# something like `Portfolio <hello@your-domain.com>` once a domain is verified.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Portfolio <hello@your-domain.com>

# Test-only. Overrides the Resend endpoint so the integration can be pointed at
# a mock server. Leave unset in production.
# RESEND_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010/emails